---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
const effectiveDate = "May 1, 2026";
const lastUpdated = "May 1, 2026";
---

<Base title="Advertiser Policy | GoDoDaytona" subtitle="Standards, disclosure requirements, and terms for all paid advertising and partnership placements on GoDoDaytona." cityBase="daytona">
  <div class="lgWrap">

    <nav class="lgBread" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/daytona/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
      <a href="/daytona/legal/">Legal</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
      <span>Advertiser Policy</span>
    </nav>

    <span class="lgEyebrow">GoDoDaytona</span>
    <h1 class="lgTitle">Advertiser Policy</h1>
    <div class="lgMeta">
      <span>Effective: {effectiveDate}</span>
      <span>Last Updated: {lastUpdated}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="lgDivider"></div>

    <div class="lgNotice">
      <p>By submitting or placing an advertisement with GoDoDaytona, you agree to the terms below. Questions? Email <a href="mailto:ads@godocity.com">ads@godocity.com</a></p>
    </div>

    <nav class="lgToc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p class="lgTocTitle">Contents</p>
      <ol class="lgTocList">
        <li><a href="#overview">1. Overview</a></li>
        <li><a href="#featured">2. Featured Ads & Paid Sponsorships</a></li>
        <li><a href="#standards">3. Ad Standards & Acceptable Content</a></li>
        <li><a href="#prohibited">4. Prohibited Content</a></li>
        <li><a href="#ftc">5. FTC Disclosure Compliance</a></li>
        <li><a href="#refusal">6. Right to Refuse or Remove</a></li>
        <li><a href="#review">7. Content Review & Approval</a></li>
        <li><a href="#payment">8. Payment & Cancellation</a></li>
        <li><a href="#performance">9. Performance & Results</a></li>
        <li><a href="#contact">10. Contact</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <div class="lgSection" id="overview">
      <h2>1. Overview</h2>
      <p>GoDoDaytona accepts advertising and community partnership arrangements across several formats: newsletter placements, social media posts, digital display advertising, and branded editorial content. All advertising is handled directly through our team.</p>
      <p>Advertising with GoDoDaytona is a commercial transaction. It does not purchase editorial coverage, inclusion in independent editorial roundups, or favorable journalistic treatment of any kind. For a clear explanation of the separation between advertising and editorial at GoDoDaytona, see our <a href="/daytona/legal/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="lgSection" id="featured">
      <h2>2. Featured Ads & Paid Sponsorships</h2>
      <p>Several of GoDoDaytona's advertising products use editorial-style formats, including branded articles and curated content placements. This section explains exactly what these products are.</p>
      <h3>Sponsored Editorial Products</h3>
      <p>The Local Spotlight (Mini Article) and The Deep Dive (Feature Article) are <strong>paid sponsorships</strong>. This means:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>These placements are purchased by the advertiser at the rates listed in our media kit.</li>
        <li>Content is produced by GoDoDaytona's editorial team and shaped around the advertiser's message, story, or offer.</li>
        <li>All such content is labeled "Sponsored," "Paid Partnership," or "Featured Partner" in accordance with FTC guidelines. This disclosure appears at or near the top of the content, before the substantive body.</li>
        <li>Payment for a sponsored content placement does not guarantee specific editorial claims, business rankings, awards language, or independent editorial endorsements.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>"Featured" Designation in Paid Placements</h3>
      <p>When the word "Featured" appears in the context of a paid advertising product or placement — including "Featured Business," "Featured Partner," or "Today's Best (Sponsored)" — it indicates a <strong>commercial arrangement</strong>, not an independent editorial recommendation. Paid "Featured" placements are always labeled as sponsored or paid.</p>
      <p>Unlabeled "Featured" mentions in GoDoDaytona editorial content represent the independent opinion of our editorial team and are not available for purchase.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="lgSection" id="standards">
      <h2>3. Ad Standards & Acceptable Content</h2>
      <p>We welcome advertising from:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Local and regional businesses serving the Daytona Beach and Volusia County market.</li>
        <li>Regional and national brands relevant to our community audience.</li>
        <li>Event organizers, nonprofits, civic organizations, and governmental agencies.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>All advertising must:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Accurately represent the advertiser's business, product, or service.</li>
        <li>Comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws and regulations.</li>
        <li>Include all legally required disclosures (e.g., contractor license numbers, financial disclaimers, healthcare caveats).</li>
        <li>Not be misleading, deceptive, or make unsubstantiated claims.</li>
        <li>Deliver to a functioning landing page that accurately reflects the advertised offer.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="lgSection" id="prohibited">
      <h2>4. Prohibited Content</h2>
      <p>GoDoDaytona does not accept advertising that:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Promotes illegal products, services, or activities under federal, Florida, or Volusia County law.</li>
        <li>Contains adult content, explicit imagery, graphic violence, or material inappropriate for a general community audience.</li>
        <li>Advertises tobacco products, e-cigarettes, vaping products, or cannabis (regardless of local legality).</li>
        <li>Promotes payday loans, predatory lending, title loans, bail bonds, or financial products with deceptive terms.</li>
        <li>Contains false, misleading, or unsubstantiated health, safety, or financial claims.</li>
        <li>Attacks, demeans, or disparages competitors, public figures, private individuals, or protected groups.</li>
        <li>Discriminates in any way on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, or age.</li>
        <li>Promotes multi-level marketing, pyramid schemes, or fraudulent investment opportunities.</li>
        <li>Contains malware, spyware, auto-playing audio, or deceptive redirect behavior.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>This list is not exhaustive. GoDoDaytona reserves the right to reject advertising for any reason consistent with our community standards.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="lgSection" id="ftc">
      <h2>5. FTC Disclosure Compliance</h2>
      <p>All sponsored and paid partnership content published by GoDoDaytona carries clear disclosures in compliance with the Federal Trade Commission's Guides Concerning the Use of Endorsements and Testimonials in Advertising (16 C.F.R. Part 255).</p>
      <p>Advertisers who provide testimonials, customer reviews, or third-party endorsements in their submitted creative are solely responsible for ensuring those claims comply with FTC guidance, including material connection disclosures where applicable.</p>
      <p>GoDoDaytona will apply our standard sponsorship disclosures to all paid content we produce. Advertisers may not request removal or modification of required disclosure language.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="lgSection" id="refusal">
      <h2>6. Right to Refuse or Remove</h2>
      <p>GoDoDaytona reserves the right to refuse, modify, postpone, suspend, or permanently remove any advertisement at our sole discretion and without liability, including if:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>The ad does not comply with this policy or our community standards.</li>
        <li>The advertiser's business has been subject to regulatory action, significant unresolved consumer complaints, or legal proceedings that we determine create reputational risk for our readers.</li>
        <li>The creative is factually inaccurate, deceptive, or misleading in our judgment.</li>
        <li>The advertiser engages in conduct inconsistent with GoDoDaytona's values.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>In the event of removal, we will notify the advertiser and provide a prorated refund for undelivered placements where applicable.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="lgSection" id="review">
      <h2>7. Content Review & Approval</h2>
      <p>All creative assets — including images, copy, links, and landing pages — must be submitted to our team at least:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>3 business days</strong> before the requested run date for newsletter and social placements.</li>
        <li><strong>5 business days</strong> before the requested run date for digital display and sponsored editorial content.</li>
        <li><strong>7 business days</strong> for feature articles (The Deep Dive), to allow for research, writing, editing, and advertiser review.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may request edits to creative that does not meet our standards. Advertisers will be given the opportunity to revise and resubmit. If revised creative is not received before the run date, the placement may be rescheduled at no penalty or refunded.</p>
      <p>For sponsored editorial products, the advertiser will receive a draft for review before publication. We welcome factual corrections and minor editorial clarifications. We do not accept changes that compromise factual accuracy or remove required disclosures.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="lgSection" id="payment">
      <h2>8. Payment & Cancellation</h2>
      <p>Payment is due in advance of the run date unless a separate invoicing arrangement has been agreed upon in writing by both parties. We accept payment by credit card, ACH transfer, and check.</p>
      <h3>Cancellations</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Cancellations made <strong>more than 72 hours</strong> before the scheduled run date receive a full credit toward a future placement.</li>
        <li>Cancellations made <strong>within 72 hours</strong> of the run date may be subject to a cancellation fee equal to 50% of the placement cost.</li>
        <li>Sponsored editorial content (The Local Spotlight, The Deep Dive) that has already entered production may not be cancelled without charge after the editorial process has begun.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Credits are valid for 12 months from the date of issuance and are non-transferable.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="lgSection" id="performance">
      <h2>9. Performance & Results</h2>
      <p>GoDoDaytona makes no guarantee of specific clicks, impressions, leads, conversions, sales, or return on investment from any placement. Advertising performance varies based on creative quality, offer strength, timing, market conditions, and audience behavior — all factors outside our direct control.</p>
      <p>Where available, we provide performance reporting data (opens, clicks, impressions) upon request following the conclusion of a campaign. Reporting data is provided for informational purposes and does not constitute a warranty of performance.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="lgSection" id="contact">
      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <p>Advertising inquiries and campaign questions:</p>
      <p><strong>GoDoDaytona Advertising</strong><br><a href="mailto:ads@godocity.com">ads@godocity.com</a></p>
      <p>Policy questions:</p>
      <p><a href="mailto:hello@gododaytona.com">hello@gododaytona.com</a></p>
      <p>To view our full advertising product menu, visit the <a href="/daytona/advertise/">Advertise</a> page.</p>
    </div>

  </div>
</Base>

